  "conclusion": "Across a century and a half, organic architecture shifts from hand-crafted nature metaphors to experimentally discovered structures and, finally, to digitally controlled continuities. Gaudí, Otto, Hundertwasser, and Hadid each insist that curvature is not mere style: it is a claim that buildings can align with the logics of bodies, landscapes, and forces. Their legacy is a modern built world increasingly comfortable with forms that look less manufactured—and more alive."
